1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,291
<i>Source Dragons!</i>

2
00:00:04,291 --> 00:00:08,208
<i>You refuse me</i>
<i>my rightful place among you,</i>

3
00:00:08,208 --> 00:00:13,250
<i>but ThunderFang</i>
<i>will not be denied!</i>

4
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:14,375
[roaring]

5
00:00:14,375 --> 00:00:16,958
[roar reverberating]

6
00:00:16,958 --> 00:00:20,041
<i>I will force myself</i>
<i>into your ranks,</i>

7
00:00:20,041 --> 00:00:24,833
<i>and you will all pay</i>
<i>for your rejection of me!</i>

8
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:27,791
[thunderous roaring]

9
00:00:27,791 --> 00:00:29,208
[Lloyd groaning]

10
00:00:29,208 --> 00:00:30,541
We gotta get
the Unbidden Storm

11
00:00:30,541 --> 00:00:32,666
working again.

12
00:00:32,666 --> 00:00:33,916
[Arin] It's impossible,

13
00:00:33,916 --> 00:00:36,125
that thing's been spinning
for centuries.

14
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:39,041
I told you I'd find a way
to mess this up.

15
00:00:39,041 --> 00:00:41,666
[Lloyd] I'm the one who caused
the cave-in, Arin, not you,

16
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:42,958
and remember,

17
00:00:42,958 --> 00:00:44,250
Ninja never quit.

18
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:46,333
I'm not a Ninja anymore.

19
00:00:47,958 --> 00:00:51,041
There's gotta be a way
to activate this thing again.

20
00:00:55,041 --> 00:00:58,375
[♪♪♪]

21
00:00:58,375 --> 00:00:59,750
This plan only works

22
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:02,000
with two halves of the dragon
combining

23
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,916
where the Unbidden Storm is.

24
00:01:03,916 --> 00:01:06,208
Let's hope
everyone else did their part.

25
00:01:06,208 --> 00:01:09,125
So... we just sit here
and wait to see

26
00:01:09,125 --> 00:01:10,833
if ThunderFang
destroys everything?

27
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:11,833
[sighing]

28
00:01:11,833 --> 00:01:12,833
Don't like this one bit.

29
00:01:14,916 --> 00:01:16,333
[gasping]

30
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,916
I guess if these crystals
are glowing,

31
00:01:23,916 --> 00:01:26,583
our half of the Arc Dragon
is still activated?

32
00:01:26,583 --> 00:01:28,375
Which is good, right?

33
00:01:28,375 --> 00:01:30,000
This is like flying blind.

34
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,208
We have no way of knowing

35
00:01:31,208 --> 00:01:33,458
if the other teams succeeded.

36
00:01:35,750 --> 00:01:37,166
[Sora] Kur?

37
00:01:38,708 --> 00:01:41,083
Spectral Dragonians? Here?

38
00:01:41,083 --> 00:01:43,166
This doesn't bode well
for the overall plan.

39
00:01:43,166 --> 00:01:46,208
Well, fighting
is more fun than planning.

40
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:51,416
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

41
00:01:51,416 --> 00:01:54,375
♪ Together we will rise ♪

42
00:01:54,375 --> 00:01:57,833
♪ We fight ♪

43
00:01:57,833 --> 00:02:00,916
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

44
00:02:02,125 --> 00:02:03,125
[thunderclap]

45
00:02:06,166 --> 00:02:07,916
I thought this was too easy.

46
00:02:07,916 --> 00:02:10,458
We had to feed birds
who were secretly bells.

47
00:02:10,458 --> 00:02:12,416
How is any of this easy?

48
00:02:12,416 --> 00:02:14,000
I mean,
I need someone to fight.

49
00:02:15,875 --> 00:02:18,041
[grunting with effort]

50
00:02:18,041 --> 00:02:19,083
[unearthly shrieking]

51
00:02:21,041 --> 00:02:22,708
[Kai grunting with effort]

52
00:02:25,083 --> 00:02:26,166
Unh!

53
00:02:26,166 --> 00:02:27,208
H'yah!

54
00:02:28,208 --> 00:02:30,083
H'yah!

55
00:02:30,083 --> 00:02:33,875
The problem with being
a backup copy of the Sorceress,

56
00:02:33,875 --> 00:02:35,708
can't do magic.

57
00:02:35,708 --> 00:02:38,375
I'm kind of useless in a fight.

58
00:02:38,375 --> 00:02:39,875
Ooh, wait!

59
00:02:39,875 --> 00:02:42,250
-[unearthly shrieking]
-Haah!

60
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:44,041
I've got it!

61
00:02:44,041 --> 00:02:45,250
Throw me!

62
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:46,375
You sure?

63
00:02:46,375 --> 00:02:48,041
It takes a lot
to hurt a coconut.

64
00:02:48,041 --> 00:02:49,041
Do it!

65
00:02:49,041 --> 00:02:50,833
[grunting with effort]

66
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,541
Yee-haw!

67
00:02:52,541 --> 00:02:54,500
Whoo-hoo-hoo!

68
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:55,875
Yes!

69
00:02:55,875 --> 00:02:58,250
Look, Ma, no hands!

70
00:02:58,250 --> 00:03:00,500
Whoo-hoo! This is
the most exciting thing

71
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:02,916
that's ever happened
to this version of me!

72
00:03:02,916 --> 00:03:05,250
Y'ah! H'yah! H'ah!

73
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,666
H'yah!

74
00:03:07,666 --> 00:03:10,125
ThunderFang really did
a number on you all.

75
00:03:10,125 --> 00:03:11,333
Hope this frees your souls!

76
00:03:11,333 --> 00:03:12,416
H'yah!

77
00:03:12,416 --> 00:03:13,958
[Nya grunting with effort]

78
00:03:15,916 --> 00:03:17,458
[stamping]

79
00:03:18,416 --> 00:03:19,500
H'yah!

80
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,708
Zarkt's going to destroy
those crystals!

81
00:03:21,708 --> 00:03:24,625
Then those crystals
must affect the Arc Dragon!

82
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:28,916
H'ah!

83
00:03:29,333 --> 00:03:30,333
[roaring]

84
00:03:30,333 --> 00:03:32,458
Let's hope this still works.

85
00:03:32,458 --> 00:03:34,583
-[unearthly shrieking]
-Hup! H'yah!

86
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:36,416
How?

87
00:03:36,416 --> 00:03:37,458
[Frak] Imperium tech.

88
00:03:40,375 --> 00:03:41,416
H'yah!

89
00:03:41,416 --> 00:03:43,458
I know Imperium's changed...

90
00:03:43,458 --> 00:03:44,625
[unearthly shrieking]

91
00:03:44,625 --> 00:03:45,875
...but just hearing those words

92
00:03:45,875 --> 00:03:47,250
still gives me a chill.

93
00:03:47,250 --> 00:03:49,208
[♪♪♪]

94
00:03:52,125 --> 00:03:53,833
[stamping]

95
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:55,333
[Wyldfyre grunting with effort]

96
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:57,333
Ugly over there
is going to Shatterspin!

97
00:03:57,333 --> 00:03:59,750
[♪♪♪]

98
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,000
[roaring]

99
00:04:06,958 --> 00:04:09,791
ThunderFang's gotten
almost all the power

100
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:10,916
out of those things.

101
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:14,583
Come on, work!

102
00:04:17,958 --> 00:04:18,916
[groaning]

103
00:04:18,916 --> 00:04:20,833
It's no use!

104
00:04:20,833 --> 00:04:22,166
I wonder if...

105
00:04:22,166 --> 00:04:23,416
Hmm.

106
00:04:27,291 --> 00:04:29,583
Not sure leaving your mech's
a good idea.

107
00:04:29,583 --> 00:04:32,000
Dragonians could be here
any second.

108
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,875
Just let me try something.

109
00:04:33,875 --> 00:04:35,541
[exhaling deeply]

110
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:39,250
Give me the Unbidden Storm!

111
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:41,000
Huh? How?

112
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,208
Just toss it!

113
00:04:45,416 --> 00:04:47,291
[roaring battle cry]

114
00:04:49,583 --> 00:04:50,666
Whoa...

115
00:04:54,333 --> 00:04:55,791
I had no idea

116
00:04:55,791 --> 00:04:57,708
you could transfer
your Object Spinjitzu

117
00:04:57,708 --> 00:04:59,791
so... intensely.

118
00:04:59,791 --> 00:05:01,833
That makes two of us,

119
00:05:01,833 --> 00:05:03,166
but I've been training,

120
00:05:03,166 --> 00:05:04,958
and it seemed like
our only option.

121
00:05:09,083 --> 00:05:10,500
Now, let's finish the job.

122
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,791
Let's hope the other teams
pulled off their part.

123
00:05:12,791 --> 00:05:15,708
[♪♪♪]

124
00:05:35,791 --> 00:05:39,416
<i>[Arc Dragon of Focus]</i>
<i>ThunderFang, we meet again.</i>

125
00:05:39,416 --> 00:05:41,541
<i>[ThunderFang]</i>
<i>If you have been sent here</i>

126
00:05:41,541 --> 00:05:43,166
<i>to challenge me,</i>

127
00:05:43,166 --> 00:05:46,583
<i>the Source Dragons</i>
<i>must truly be afraid.</i>

128
00:05:47,916 --> 00:05:50,583
Why does everything look weird?

129
00:05:50,583 --> 00:05:55,125
Are you also seeing, like,
a vision or something?

130
00:05:55,125 --> 00:05:56,416
<i>[ThunderFang snarling]</i>

131
00:05:58,500 --> 00:05:59,833
We're each seeing through
the eyes

132
00:05:59,833 --> 00:06:02,708
of one of
the Arc Dragon's heads!

133
00:06:04,041 --> 00:06:07,083
<i>[ThunderFang] You may have</i>
<i>bested me last time,</i>

134
00:06:07,083 --> 00:06:12,333
<i>but now I am more powerful</i>
<i>than I have ever been!</i>

135
00:06:12,333 --> 00:06:13,875
[roaring]

136
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:18,916
[cheering] Wa-hoo-hoo-hoo!
Right in the poppa!

137
00:06:25,416 --> 00:06:26,625
[dragon roaring]

138
00:06:26,625 --> 00:06:27,666
[Nya] Hey, ugly!

139
00:06:27,666 --> 00:06:28,833
Made you look.

140
00:06:29,958 --> 00:06:31,916
[dragon roaring]

141
00:06:31,916 --> 00:06:33,041
ThunderFang!

142
00:06:33,041 --> 00:06:34,208
[unearthly shrieking]

143
00:06:34,208 --> 00:06:36,083
[Kai grunting with effort]

144
00:06:36,083 --> 00:06:37,416
[Kai] How are we seeing that?

145
00:06:37,416 --> 00:06:38,791
[Nya] We were right.

146
00:06:38,791 --> 00:06:41,666
These crystals are connected
to the Focus Dragon.

147
00:06:41,666 --> 00:06:44,458
I think we're seeing
through the dragon's eyes!

148
00:06:44,458 --> 00:06:46,333
[roaring]

149
00:06:51,791 --> 00:06:53,416
[snoring]

150
00:06:56,916 --> 00:06:57,958
[unearthly shrieking]

151
00:06:57,958 --> 00:06:59,833
[grunting with effort]

152
00:07:01,041 --> 00:07:03,250
This is called
a set-up! Yaah!

153
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,041
[roaring]

154
00:07:07,875 --> 00:07:08,875
<i>[ThunderFang roaring]</i>

155
00:07:10,083 --> 00:07:12,041
...and that's called
the pay-off!

156
00:07:12,041 --> 00:07:13,083
[unearthly shrieking]

157
00:07:13,083 --> 00:07:15,750
[Frak grunting with effort]

158
00:07:18,208 --> 00:07:21,166
[dream chorus chiming]

159
00:07:23,291 --> 00:07:25,625
Sora, in case
we don't get out of this,

160
00:07:25,625 --> 00:07:27,041
there's something
I need to tell you.

161
00:07:28,083 --> 00:07:30,458
-What?
-I... um... I...

162
00:07:30,458 --> 00:07:32,875
ate all the yogurt
in the monastery fridge.

163
00:07:32,875 --> 00:07:34,125
[grunting with impact]

164
00:07:34,125 --> 00:07:35,583
You... what?

165
00:07:35,583 --> 00:07:36,583
I confess.

166
00:07:36,583 --> 00:07:38,166
All of it, it's gone.

167
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,750
Great.

168
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:40,750
You're forgiven.

169
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:42,000
Why did I need to know this now?

170
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,500
Um, in case you make it out
and I don't,

171
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:46,333
and later somebody wonders
where all the yogurt went,

172
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:47,708
you'll have
a definitive answer.

173
00:07:47,708 --> 00:07:50,750
[panting] Okay... weirdo.

174
00:07:50,750 --> 00:07:52,625
[stamping]

175
00:07:52,625 --> 00:07:54,333
[Sora] Kur's trying
Shatterspin again!

176
00:07:54,333 --> 00:07:55,708
[Frak] Wyldfyre, heads up!

177
00:07:55,708 --> 00:07:57,000
[unearthly shrieking]

178
00:07:58,458 --> 00:08:00,833
I am not giving this back.

179
00:08:00,833 --> 00:08:01,916
Keepsies!

180
00:08:01,916 --> 00:08:03,791
[spin rumbling]

181
00:08:04,666 --> 00:08:05,916
Yaah!

182
00:08:07,875 --> 00:08:09,208
[stamping]

183
00:08:09,208 --> 00:08:10,041
[groaning]

184
00:08:11,041 --> 00:08:12,166
[stamping]

185
00:08:12,166 --> 00:08:13,458
[Sora] No!

186
00:08:14,541 --> 00:08:15,625
Ah! Oof!

187
00:08:17,125 --> 00:08:17,958
H'yah!

188
00:08:22,583 --> 00:08:23,583
[roaring]

189
00:08:28,375 --> 00:08:29,250
<i>[ThunderFang crying out]</i>

190
00:08:31,875 --> 00:08:35,625
<i>[ThunderFang] You're nothing</i>
<i>but a lapdog of the Sources!</i>

191
00:08:35,625 --> 00:08:39,666
<i>Puppet of corrupt masters!</i>

192
00:08:39,666 --> 00:08:42,958
<i>I will soon be</i>
<i>the Eighth Source,</i>

193
00:08:42,958 --> 00:08:45,416
<i>and I will rain chaos</i>

194
00:08:45,416 --> 00:08:47,958
<i>across the Merged Lands!</i>

195
00:08:47,958 --> 00:08:48,791
[gasping]

196
00:08:50,291 --> 00:08:52,041
[groaning]

197
00:08:52,041 --> 00:08:53,291
[gasping]

198
00:08:53,291 --> 00:08:56,125
I'm not just seeing
what the Focus Dragon sees,

199
00:08:56,125 --> 00:08:58,500
I'm feeling what it feels,

200
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,458
and it hurts!

201
00:08:59,458 --> 00:09:02,333
Yeah, didn't need
any more pain,

202
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:06,250
but does it feel like
the dragon wants our help?

203
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:08,500
Yeah, I sense it too.

204
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,166
Follow my lead.

205
00:09:14,208 --> 00:09:15,083
[growling]

206
00:09:23,416 --> 00:09:24,333
[growling]

207
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:26,083
[grunting in pain]

208
00:09:29,208 --> 00:09:30,458
[groaning]

209
00:09:30,458 --> 00:09:31,958
You okay?

210
00:09:31,958 --> 00:09:35,041
[grunting] I got this. Come on.

211
00:09:40,541 --> 00:09:41,958
[gasping]

212
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:44,333
Yaah!

213
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:45,208
Oof!

214
00:09:48,916 --> 00:09:50,041
[reverberating roar]

215
00:09:53,583 --> 00:09:55,041
[both grunting with effort]

216
00:10:00,166 --> 00:10:01,375
[roaring]

217
00:10:05,083 --> 00:10:06,708
[groaning]

218
00:10:06,708 --> 00:10:07,833
[ThunderFang snarling]

219
00:10:09,458 --> 00:10:10,791
[grunting with effort]

220
00:10:10,791 --> 00:10:12,458
H'ah! H'ah! H'ah! H'ah!

221
00:10:12,458 --> 00:10:16,000
[grunting and straining]

222
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,541
Lloyd, I'm trying to stay
in sync with you,

223
00:10:17,541 --> 00:10:18,625
but-- [grunting]

224
00:10:18,625 --> 00:10:19,625
[roaring]

225
00:10:22,416 --> 00:10:24,375
[panting]

226
00:10:26,916 --> 00:10:28,333
[groaning]

227
00:10:28,333 --> 00:10:30,708
[Lloyd] This isn't working.

228
00:10:30,708 --> 00:10:33,458
The pain... I can't focus.

229
00:10:33,458 --> 00:10:36,375
This is when you would tell me
Ninja never quit.

230
00:10:36,375 --> 00:10:38,291
[groaning] We don't,

231
00:10:38,291 --> 00:10:41,583
but we know when it's time
to change the plan.

232
00:10:41,583 --> 00:10:43,875
Arin, you take the lead.

233
00:10:43,875 --> 00:10:45,541
I'll follow you.

234
00:10:45,541 --> 00:10:46,833
No. No way!

235
00:10:46,833 --> 00:10:48,541
The Merged Lands
are at stake here.

236
00:10:48,541 --> 00:10:50,041
I mess everything up!

237
00:10:50,041 --> 00:10:51,416
You can do this.

238
00:10:51,416 --> 00:10:52,875
Just focus.

239
00:10:52,875 --> 00:10:54,666
Trust me, Arin.

240
00:10:56,083 --> 00:10:57,750
[♪♪♪]

241
00:10:58,583 --> 00:11:00,416
[neck cracking]

242
00:11:01,625 --> 00:11:03,791
[neck cracking]

243
00:11:03,791 --> 00:11:06,333
[growling]

244
00:11:08,208 --> 00:11:09,416
[roaring]

245
00:11:14,250 --> 00:11:15,291
[snarling]

246
00:11:16,458 --> 00:11:18,083
<i>Tell your masters</i>

247
00:11:18,083 --> 00:11:20,916
<i>ThunderFang will reap veng--</i>

248
00:11:22,916 --> 00:11:24,083
[ThunderFang] Aah!

249
00:11:25,083 --> 00:11:26,375
[groaning]

250
00:11:26,375 --> 00:11:29,208
<i>[Arc Dragon of Focus]</i>
<i>The battle is not over yet.</i>

251
00:11:29,208 --> 00:11:31,000
[grunting with effort]

252
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:31,916
Waah!

253
00:11:31,916 --> 00:11:32,916
Oof!

254
00:11:32,916 --> 00:11:34,583
Haah! Haah! Hi-yah!

255
00:11:37,416 --> 00:11:38,416
[panting]

256
00:11:38,416 --> 00:11:40,625
That all you got?

257
00:11:40,625 --> 00:11:42,958
Aah! Whoa!

258
00:11:42,958 --> 00:11:43,916
[gasping]

259
00:11:43,916 --> 00:11:46,333
[Zarkt shrieking]

260
00:11:46,333 --> 00:11:47,666
Nya!

261
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:48,833
[Nya shrieking]

262
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:49,916
[Kai shouting]

263
00:11:49,916 --> 00:11:52,083
Haah! Aah!

264
00:11:52,083 --> 00:11:54,000
[grunting with effort]

265
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,541
[unearthly shrieking]

266
00:11:55,541 --> 00:11:56,541
[yelping]

267
00:11:56,541 --> 00:11:58,375
[panting]

268
00:11:58,375 --> 00:11:59,916
[spectral shrieking]

269
00:11:59,916 --> 00:12:00,916
No!

270
00:12:04,083 --> 00:12:06,625
Boo-yah! Take that!

271
00:12:06,625 --> 00:12:09,375
[gasping] Jay?

272
00:12:09,375 --> 00:12:11,666
You're one of my least
favorite people, Zarkt.

273
00:12:14,708 --> 00:12:18,041
[♪♪♪]

274
00:12:26,666 --> 00:12:29,458
Aah... haah!

275
00:12:36,166 --> 00:12:39,041
I knew you'd come back, Jay.

276
00:12:39,041 --> 00:12:41,000
I-I just happened
to be in the area.

277
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:42,625
[chuckling]

278
00:12:42,625 --> 00:12:45,375
You just happened
to be deep in a cave

279
00:12:45,375 --> 00:12:47,625
hidden behind
a magical waterfall?

280
00:12:47,625 --> 00:12:48,958
Maybe. You don't know.

281
00:12:48,958 --> 00:12:52,083
I could be really into caves,

282
00:12:52,083 --> 00:12:53,125
or...

283
00:12:53,125 --> 00:12:54,666
maybe you said some things

284
00:12:54,666 --> 00:12:56,666
that stuck with me.

285
00:12:56,666 --> 00:12:59,375
I don't remember you,

286
00:12:59,375 --> 00:13:01,583
but being with you

287
00:13:01,583 --> 00:13:03,000
makes me want to be...

288
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,875
not a terrible person.

289
00:13:07,291 --> 00:13:08,375
[gasping]

290
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:13,458
[Kai grunting with effort]

291
00:13:14,541 --> 00:13:17,041
Jay! That was amazing!

292
00:13:17,041 --> 00:13:18,500
Forget everything I used to say

293
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:19,875
about you being the worst Ninja!

294
00:13:19,875 --> 00:13:21,791
You used to say what?

295
00:13:21,791 --> 00:13:23,583
Huh? What?
No, no, that was Cole.

296
00:13:23,583 --> 00:13:24,541
We should go.

297
00:13:24,541 --> 00:13:27,041
[unearthly shrieking]

298
00:13:28,083 --> 00:13:30,041
[groaning]

299
00:13:31,875 --> 00:13:33,208
[shrieking]

300
00:13:36,041 --> 00:13:37,458
No...

301
00:13:39,541 --> 00:13:42,500
[♪♪♪]

302
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,541
[together] Riyu!

303
00:13:55,541 --> 00:13:57,916
[roaring]

304
00:14:01,666 --> 00:14:03,125
[roar reverberating]

305
00:14:08,416 --> 00:14:10,000
[grunting with effort]
H'yah! H'ah!

306
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,833
It's working!

307
00:14:15,833 --> 00:14:17,166
[snarling]

308
00:14:20,583 --> 00:14:21,833
H'ah! [blow thudding]

309
00:14:21,833 --> 00:14:23,791
H'yah! [slamming]

310
00:14:25,250 --> 00:14:26,875
<i>[ThunderFang]</i>
<i>How dare you seven</i>

311
00:14:26,875 --> 00:14:29,708
<i>keep all the power</i>
<i>for yourselves!</i>

312
00:14:29,708 --> 00:14:33,500
<i>I belong amongst</i>
<i>the Source Dragons!</i>

313
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,583
[together] Ninja...

314
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:39,375
Go!

315
00:14:39,375 --> 00:14:42,541
[♪♪♪]

316
00:14:45,333 --> 00:14:46,208
[ThunderFang groaning]

317
00:14:46,208 --> 00:14:47,791
[cheering] Yeah!

318
00:14:47,791 --> 00:14:49,041
[laughing and cheering]

319
00:14:50,208 --> 00:14:52,250
[groaning]

320
00:14:52,250 --> 00:14:54,000
Aah!

321
00:14:55,458 --> 00:14:58,083
[roaring]

322
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,750
[muttering] Janet... Janet...

323
00:15:12,625 --> 00:15:14,375
Aah! Whaa?

324
00:15:14,375 --> 00:15:16,500
How did I get here?

325
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,125
Janet!

326
00:15:18,125 --> 00:15:20,583
[♪♪♪]

327
00:15:20,583 --> 00:15:22,916
[gasping in wonder]

328
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:27,000
[all gasping]

329
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:30,458
Well, these forms
aren't gonna stamp themselves.

330
00:15:30,458 --> 00:15:31,958
[♪♪♪]

331
00:15:33,250 --> 00:15:35,750
It's good
we're not hollow anymore.

332
00:15:35,750 --> 00:15:36,750
Yeah, seriously.

333
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:37,958
Can you imagine

334
00:15:37,958 --> 00:15:39,583
just mindlessly stumbling
through life like that?

335
00:15:42,416 --> 00:15:43,666
[moaning]

336
00:15:44,666 --> 00:15:46,416
Whoa! [sighing]

337
00:15:46,416 --> 00:15:48,416
Yeah, I feel like
I missed something.

338
00:15:51,250 --> 00:15:53,083
[all gasping in delight]

339
00:15:53,083 --> 00:15:55,000
[laughing happily]

340
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,000
[Lee] Friends!

341
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,541
I've been a bad neighbor.

342
00:15:58,541 --> 00:16:00,416
I've lied to you,

343
00:16:00,416 --> 00:16:03,541
and it's time
I tell you all the truth...

344
00:16:03,541 --> 00:16:05,791
[♪♪♪]

345
00:16:09,083 --> 00:16:12,041
[gasping and groaning]

346
00:16:12,041 --> 00:16:13,458
Fritz!

347
00:16:13,458 --> 00:16:15,625
Spitz! Bonzle!

348
00:16:15,625 --> 00:16:17,125
You're okay!

349
00:16:17,125 --> 00:16:19,333
[♪♪♪]

350
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:31,916
[Arin] ThunderFang's gone?

351
00:16:31,916 --> 00:16:32,958
We did it?

352
00:16:32,958 --> 00:16:35,625
You did it, Arin.

353
00:16:35,625 --> 00:16:37,250
<i>[Arc Dragon of Focus]</i>
<i>You did well, mortals...</i>

354
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:41,083
<i>in waking me from my slumber,</i>

355
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:43,250
<i>and guiding me with your focus.</i>

356
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:45,208
What'd I say?

357
00:16:45,208 --> 00:16:46,333
<i>[Arc Dragon of Focus] However,</i>

358
00:16:46,333 --> 00:16:50,208
<i>my masters</i>
<i>may not feel the same way.</i>

359
00:16:50,208 --> 00:16:52,958
<i>I return now to my slumber,</i>

360
00:16:52,958 --> 00:16:56,750
<i>and pray the consequences</i>
<i>for your actions</i>

361
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:59,416
<i>are not too dire.</i>

362
00:17:04,916 --> 00:17:08,166
Well... that sounded ominous.

363
00:17:08,166 --> 00:17:10,833
Arin, during the fight,

364
00:17:10,833 --> 00:17:13,958
I was trying to force things
to go the way I wanted,

365
00:17:13,958 --> 00:17:15,500
to control it all,

366
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:18,208
but now I realize,

367
00:17:18,208 --> 00:17:20,958
I need to let go sometimes,

368
00:17:20,958 --> 00:17:24,750
which also means...
letting go of you.

369
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:28,166
I can't force you
to become a Ninja, Arin.

370
00:17:28,166 --> 00:17:29,291
[sighing heavily]

371
00:17:29,291 --> 00:17:30,958
You don't have to, Lloyd,

372
00:17:30,958 --> 00:17:33,541
because, after all this,

373
00:17:33,541 --> 00:17:35,291
I realize I already am.

374
00:17:35,291 --> 00:17:37,708
[♪♪♪]

375
00:17:39,083 --> 00:17:42,000
If that's still okay with you.

376
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,708
[Lloyd] There's nothing
I want more.

377
00:17:45,958 --> 00:17:47,625
[snoring]

378
00:17:47,625 --> 00:17:49,416
[sighing] Still exhausted

379
00:17:49,416 --> 00:17:51,875
from creating
that Arc Dragon, I see.

380
00:17:51,875 --> 00:17:53,000
I feel them.

381
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,708
I could sleep for a week.

382
00:17:54,708 --> 00:17:57,916
But Zanth is kinda...
our ride home.

383
00:17:57,916 --> 00:17:59,458
We have other options.

384
00:18:01,083 --> 00:18:03,541
The Monastery Gates, of course!

385
00:18:03,541 --> 00:18:05,250
[low rumbling]

386
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:06,291
Whoa.

387
00:18:06,291 --> 00:18:08,583
I'm suddenly light-headed
or something.

388
00:18:08,583 --> 00:18:11,458
I feel weird too.

389
00:18:11,458 --> 00:18:13,875
Is Djinjago tilting?

390
00:18:13,875 --> 00:18:16,250
No, but something's off.

391
00:18:19,666 --> 00:18:21,208
[low rumbling]

392
00:18:21,208 --> 00:18:22,916
[Nya groaning]

393
00:18:22,916 --> 00:18:25,208
[all groaning]

394
00:18:25,208 --> 00:18:27,416
[Arin] ...but before
I get back to training,

395
00:18:27,416 --> 00:18:29,583
I need a vacation
with my parents.

396
00:18:29,583 --> 00:18:31,583
It's been so long.

397
00:18:31,583 --> 00:18:32,666
Absolutely--

398
00:18:32,666 --> 00:18:33,958
[groaning]

399
00:18:33,958 --> 00:18:34,875
[low rumbling]

400
00:18:34,875 --> 00:18:36,166
Are you okay?

401
00:18:36,166 --> 00:18:37,583
[gasping]

402
00:18:37,583 --> 00:18:39,666
I feel weird.

403
00:18:39,666 --> 00:18:42,083
It's like my connection...

404
00:18:42,083 --> 00:18:43,958
My elemental power.

405
00:18:46,916 --> 00:18:49,000
Something's wrong with it.

406
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,083
What would cause that?

407
00:18:50,083 --> 00:18:51,208
I don't know,

408
00:18:51,208 --> 00:18:53,416
but we need to get back
to the Monastery...

409
00:18:53,416 --> 00:18:54,541
now.

410
00:18:54,541 --> 00:18:57,166
[♪♪♪]

411
00:18:57,166 --> 00:18:58,166
[together] Ninjago!

412
00:18:58,166 --> 00:19:00,875
[♪♪♪]

413
00:19:12,958 --> 00:19:14,500
[gasping]

414
00:19:15,541 --> 00:19:17,750
This isn't right.

415
00:19:23,625 --> 00:19:24,958
Whoa...

416
00:19:24,958 --> 00:19:27,375
We're not in Ninjago.

417
00:19:33,541 --> 00:19:36,958
Uh, the Gate took us
to the wrong place.

418
00:19:36,958 --> 00:19:39,166
[door creaking shut]

419
00:19:40,083 --> 00:19:41,250
[grunting with effort]

420
00:19:41,250 --> 00:19:42,458
Why isn't it opening?

421
00:19:42,458 --> 00:19:43,458
[locked handle rattling]

422
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:46,500
[pounding]

423
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:47,708
We're stranded here.

424
00:19:50,041 --> 00:19:51,541
How could this happen?

425
00:19:57,166 --> 00:19:58,583
[rattling]

426
00:19:58,583 --> 00:20:03,541
Your former students
are lost now, old man,

427
00:20:03,541 --> 00:20:05,791
scattered across
the farthest reaches

428
00:20:05,791 --> 00:20:07,666
of the Merged Lands.

429
00:20:07,666 --> 00:20:09,125
[rattling and banging]

430
00:20:09,125 --> 00:20:12,916
Now nothing
will stand in my way.

431
00:20:18,083 --> 00:20:19,583
<i>[Energy] I would never</i>
<i>have believed</i>

432
00:20:19,583 --> 00:20:21,958
<i>our siblings would do this.</i>

433
00:20:21,958 --> 00:20:24,458
<i>Withdraw from the Council?</i>

434
00:20:24,458 --> 00:20:26,916
<i>It's unthinkable.</i>

435
00:20:26,916 --> 00:20:29,708
<i>[Flow] The mortals dared</i>
<i>command Focus's Arc Dragon,</i>

436
00:20:29,708 --> 00:20:31,666
<i>her personal avatar.</i>

437
00:20:31,666 --> 00:20:35,875
<i>Even you must admit</i>
<i>it was highly... improper.</i>

438
00:20:35,875 --> 00:20:37,625
<i>[Motion] Improper, perhaps,</i>

439
00:20:37,625 --> 00:20:41,625
<i>yet it saved this Council</i>
<i>from ThunderFang's wrath.</i>

440
00:20:41,625 --> 00:20:44,416
<i>The Conduit</i>
<i>made the right choice.</i>

441
00:20:44,416 --> 00:20:47,791
<i>[Energy] And yet it is</i>
<i>the mortals that will suffer.</i>

442
00:20:47,791 --> 00:20:51,333
<i>With Focus, Life,</i>
<i>and Strength withdrawn,</i>

443
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:54,583
<i>the balance</i>
<i>of elemental powers is askew.</i>

444
00:20:54,583 --> 00:20:56,541
<i>It will cause chaos</i>

445
00:20:56,541 --> 00:20:58,375
<i>for the powers</i>
<i>of every Elemental Master</i>

446
00:20:58,375 --> 00:21:00,583
<i>in the Merged Lands.</i>

447
00:21:00,583 --> 00:21:02,458
<i>[Flow] Our promise</i>
<i>to the First Spinjitzu Master</i>

448
00:21:02,458 --> 00:21:03,666
<i>is broken.</i>

449
00:21:03,666 --> 00:21:06,666
<i>Source Dragons</i>
<i>violating their sacred word...</i>

450
00:21:06,666 --> 00:21:09,708
<i>it may mean</i>
<i>the end of this cycle.</i>

451
00:21:09,708 --> 00:21:12,666
<i>[Motion] Not just the end</i>
<i>of this cycle,</i>

452
00:21:12,666 --> 00:21:14,458
<i>the end of all cycles.</i>

453
00:21:14,458 --> 00:21:18,458
<i>The universe has never been</i>
<i>in more danger.</i>

454
00:21:21,916 --> 00:21:23,333
[Arin] We're trapped
who knows where,

455
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:24,750
the gates stopped working,

456
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:26,458
and your powers
are all messed up.

457
00:21:26,458 --> 00:21:28,291
What are we gonna do, Lloyd?

458
00:21:28,291 --> 00:21:30,375
What Ninja always do...

459
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:37,000
[♪♪♪]

460
00:21:42,041 --> 00:21:43,916
...we'll find a way.

461
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,833
[♪♪♪]

